# 4:1 Multiplexer using Verilog HDL

## Introduction

A multiplexer (MUX) is a combinational digital circuit that selects
one input from multiple input signals and sends the selected input
to a single output.

This project implements a 4:1 multiplexer using Verilog HDL.

## Features

* 4 input lines
* 2 select lines
* 1 output line
* Combinational circuit
* Verilog HDL implementation
* Testbench included
* Simulation output included

## Folder Structure

```text
verilog-4to1-multiplexer/
│
├── src/
│   └── mux_4to1.v
│
├── tb/
│   └── mux_4to1_tb.v
